\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Solves a subcritical amplitude normal form and its diverging stationary decay length, separating onset and wavelength selection.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
The complete supplied definition, including source qualifications and the dated literature assessment, was reviewed. The calculation below is an elementary restricted attempt motivated by [S2]; it does not claim novelty or a fresh literature-status determination.

\paragraph{Context and investigated scope.} The complete supplied definition, including source qualifications and the dated literature assessment, was reviewed. The calculation below is an elementary restricted attempt motivated by [S2]; it does not claim novelty or a fresh literature-status determination.

\paragraph{A subcritical amplitude test.} Consider the real amplitude equation $\dot a=\mu a+ba^3-ca^5$ with $b,c>0$. Nonzero equilibria have $r=a^2>0$ satisfying $cr^2-br-\mu=0$. They first appear at $\mu=-b^2/(4c)$ in a saddle-node, although the zero state stays linearly stable until $\mu=0$. This elementary distinction prevents identifying the onset of sustained finite-amplitude behavior with a linear-instability threshold.

\paragraph{A large length can arise, but is not selected.} Add diffusion: $a_t=D a_{xx}+\mu a+ba^3-ca^5$, $D>0$. Linearizing a stationary profile near a stable homogeneous equilibrium $a_*$ gives $D v''+f'(a_*)v=0$, where $f(a)=\mu a+ba^3-ca^5$. Exponentially decaying perturbations have length
\[
 \ell=\sqrt{D/(-f'(a_*))}\quad\text{when }f'(a_*)<0.
\]
On the upper nonzero branch, $f'(a_*)=2r(b-2cr)$, which approaches zero from below at the saddle-node. Thus this toy interface width diverges there. It is a decay length, not automatically the wavelength of a stable pattern; the scalar equation alone can coarsen instead of selecting periodic bands.

\paragraph{Source gap.} These formulas exhibit two plausible ingredients, subcriticality and a slow relaxation length, without deriving them from Navier--Stokes or identifying $\mu$ with the source Reynolds parameter. The missing step is a controlled reduction giving coefficients, mode interactions and wavelength selection in the actual shear geometry. Neither the recurrent proximity to $R_{e,c}$ nor the observed pattern scale is thereby explained quantitatively.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked saddle-node and linear thresholds, upper-branch derivative and decay-length interpretation; did not identify scalar coarsening with stable band selection. Model self-audit only; no independent human proof checking. Prompts A and B were applied to this canonical record and its qualified source scope. Checked saddle-node and linear thresholds, upper-branch derivative and decay-length interpretation; did not identify scalar coarsening with stable band selection. Retained unresolved status and zero original-target progress; No Navier–Stokes reduction or mechanism selecting the actual turbulent-laminar wavelength is derived.

